# twin_lid_slstm.config -- Phase 9 Task 5 LID mechanical-wiring fixture (spec S8.3).
# GENERATED by scripts/extract_phase9_fixtures.py from the committed phase-4b
# twin_gradcheck.config: SAME corpus, SAME SAD net (legacy peephole LSTM), only the
# LID net swapped to the phase-9 sLSTM cell via BLSTM_LID_Cell_Type + its seed pack,
# and the inherited Neural_Networks_Gradient_Check_Epsilon line REMOVED so run() is a
# forward+backward fold at theta rather than the engine's own full gradCheck sweep.
# twin_gradcheck.config -- Phase 4b Task 9 (Algo 6, Mode 5, wav, corpus gradCheck).
# twin_mode5.config with TINY nets (every GEMM reduction dim < 23 -> the REAL compiled
# engine matches the ascending-loop port bit-for-bit), BOTH nets backprop-active (the
# gradCheck iterates network ii=0 [SAD, cost cols 4/len-1] then ii=1 [LID, cols
# 14/len-2] -- THE column switch under pin), SQUARE cost laws (polynomial -> the
# goldens are strict-bits on every platform, no libm canary), InputNormalizationType 0
# both (no self-norm), nb_DCT 0 (filterbank-only features, no Eigen DCT GEMM), and a
# 1-file wav corpus (f1.wav + f1.stm, class vie=1 so the binary-LID SAD-target zeroing
# quirk at :710 does NOT fire and the SAD targets stay reference-driven).
# Windows 0 -> plain whole-sequence FFB for both nets.
# Audio_max_duration 0.2 (21 periodogram rows): keeps EVERY backward deriv
# reduction dim (k = T) below the nn_product_probes k>=23 Eigen-blocking
# boundary, so the REAL backward == the ascending port bit-for-bit too.
